{
 "brief": "Palestinian official Motaz al-Masloukhi, head of the legal committee and general secretariat member of the Palestinian Diaspora's Popular Conference, said legal or political objections to new electoral mechanisms—including electoral colleges and consensus-building—remain legitimate and justified, Shehab Wire reported. He emphasized the need to transition from faction-based legitimacy to institutional legitimacy in National Council elections.\n\nAl-Masloukhi's comments come as Palestinian political groups dispute electoral procedures ahead of council elections.",
